# GetConnectionOfThread Method

Applies to:{.prefix}

Server{.info}

~~~
R←X GetConnectionOfThread Y
~~~

X is a server, Y is a thread number, R is the connection served by that thread, or `⍬` if there is
none.

Every connection is served by a thread of its own, so GetConnectionOfThread tells an error handler
that runs in the thread that crashed what that thread was working on. The connection's `Messages`
hold what has been received so far: complete requests, and possibly one that is only partly
received. Its `LastBlock` holds the last block of data exactly as it was received, which is what
matters most when a request is so ill-formed that it could not be parsed.

Note that both may contain credentials, for example in an "Authorization" header.

